    "imageName" : "gitlab.cosy.bio:5050/cosybio/federated-learning/federated_db/app-build-pipeline/transformer-split-rows:vElEmkSt",
    "shortDescription" : "Split two rows using a delimiter.",
    "longDescription" : "# Transformer Combine Rows\n\nTransformer Split Rows expands a CSV table by splitting delimited cell values into multiple rows.\nIt is the inverse operation of Transformer Combine Rows: instead of aggregating many rows into one,\nit takes delimited values (e.g., \"a,b,c\") and normalizes them back into row-wise form. This is\nuseful when previously combined columns (codes/labels/IDs) must be processed as individual records\nagain.\n\n## Core behavior\n\n- Reads an input CSV table.\n- If the first column is named id (case-insensitive), it is treated as an identifier column and is\n  preserved.\n- For every other column:\n- values from all rows are converted to string form (implementation-dependent),\n- then concatenated using the configured delimiter.\n- Produces a single-row output CSV.\n\n## Hyperparameter\n\n- delimiter (STRING): Separator used when concatenating values (e.g., \",\", \";\", \"|\", \"\\n\").\n\n## Input\n\n- table (CSV, required): Tabular input whose rows will be combined.\n\n## Output\n\n- combined (CSV): One-row table containing concatenated column values.\n\n## Notes / assumptions\n\n- Null/empty handling depends on the implementation (e.g., whether NaNs become empty strings or \"\n  nan\").\n- Non-string values are typically stringified before concatenation.",
    "appConfig" : {
      "hyperparams" : [ {
        "name" : "columns",
        "variableName" : "columns",
        "type" : "STRING",
        "description" : "Delimiter used to split values when expanding into rows",
        "mode" : "BOTH",
        "options" : [ ],
        "default" : "|"
      } ],
      "input" : [ {
